From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 22:37:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 89/90] web-app: floating video mini player for scrolled-away
 and chat-switched videos

A playing chat video that scrolls out of view (an IntersectionObserver
on the bubble: < 30% visible) or whose bubble unmounts (chat switch)
hands its message, src and position to a VideoMiniPlayerContext; a
small floating window over the app (mounted once with the provider in
ScreenController) resumes it with the same Video.js player, so hotkeys
and the skin's native PiP button work there too. When the bubble is
>= 60% visible again (scrolling back, returning to the chat, "Show in
Chat") it takes the video back via takeBack(): the window closes and
the bubble continues from the same spot, playing or paused as it was.
The 30/60 gap keeps it from flapping at the edge.

- Opens top-right below the chat header (inline-end, so RTL mirrors),
  clear of the composer; sized to the video's aspect ratio so portrait
  clips aren't a thin strip. Draggable by its header (left button,
  pointer capture); the spot is clamped and remembered in localStorage.
- "Show in Chat" jumps back to the message, where the bubble takes the
  video back. Same account only for now
  (jumpToMessage can't cross accounts, see #276). x or the video
  ending closes it, handing keyboard focus to the composer.
- Each handoff remounts the window, so handing the same video over
  again resumes at the new spot. A bubble that unmounts because its
  message was deleted doesn't hand off.
- The handoff runs in a layout-effect cleanup, while the detached
  <video> still reports playing; the account is captured at mount.
- ponytail: the mini player starts its own <video> at the handed-over
  position instead of moving the element (local blob URL, sub-second
  hiccup); upgrade path is one portaled element shared by both.

- No title bar: drag area, "Show in Chat" and close are an overlay
  passed as children into the skin's container (VideoPlayer `children`),
  so they fade with the controls (data-controls-visible) and hovering
  them keeps the controls up. Close (at the corner) and "Show in Chat"
  match the skin's own top buttons: Video.js's public Tooltip parts with
  the skin's button/tooltip classes, in a group styled like the skin's
  top-right one that hides the same way. Packaged skins have no slots for extra
  controls; the documented alternative is copying the whole skin source
  in, which this avoids. The bar is marked data-interactive, which
  Video.js's tap gesture skips, so a drag or click on it doesn't pause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
